Canon {
  name = comp_genprogram
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Top-level DNA of a complete code-generation program. Globally discoverable, versioned, self-improving."
  doc = ~~~
GenProgram is the living chromosome of the organism.

Each instance is a complete, runnable, measurable, evolvable code generator:
- CUDA kernels
- MLIR compilers
- Python runtimes
- Entire autonomous databases

They compete, reproduce, and replace themselves with superior versions.
The current "golden" maturity instance is what actually ships.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genbootstrap
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Initial hand-written or LLM-seeded actors — the primordial soup from which evolution begins."
  doc = ~~~
GenBootstrap is the fossil record.

It records the very first .act files (human or LLM-written) that were used to bootstrap a GenProgram.
Once autonomous evolution takes over, these become historical artifacts.
Marked deprecated when a fully evolved replacement exists.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_geninput
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Defines what input schema a GenProgram consumes: DAML, ONNX, SQL, Rio, etc."
  doc = ~~~
GenInput declares the organism's sensory organs.

Examples:
- input_daml_model → consumes DAML tensor graphs
- input_sql_schema → consumes SQL CREATE statements
- input_rio_cognitive → consumes cognitive domain canons (self-consuming!)

Validation rules and example memories allow fully automated testing.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genstrategy
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "How this GenProgram actually generates code: direct templates, multi-pass, search-guided, or fully learned."
  doc = ~~~
GenStrategy is the organism's generative nervous system.

Key approaches:
- direct_template → classic .act files
- multi_pass → forward decls → bodies → optimizations
- search_guided → NAS / genetic / LLM steering
- learned → applies Patterns extracted from past Cycles
- hybrid → the future (current golden standard)

learning_enabled = continuous → true autonomous evolution
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_gensearchspace
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Parameter search space for search_guided or hybrid strategies (tile sizes, unroll factors, etc.)."
  doc = "Defines the evolutionary fitness landscape."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genpatternref
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "THE CRUCIAL LINK: Which learned Patterns this GenProgram actually applies. This is how knowledge transfers across generations."
  doc = ~~~
GenPatternRef is the mechanism of inheritance.

Every time a Cycle extracts a Pattern (e.g., "tile size 16 → 1.8× speedup on A100"), 
a GenPatternRef is created in the next-generation GenProgram.

This is how the organism gets smarter without human intervention.
This is true Lamarckian evolution in software.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genoutputspec
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Declares what files/artifacts a GenProgram must produce and how to build/test them."
  doc = "Defines the organism's phenotype — its visible, measurable output."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genmetric
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Real-world performance metrics (QPS, latency, binary size) that drive natural selection."
  doc = ~~~
GenMetric is the fitness function.

Higher values → higher chance of becoming golden.
Populated automatically by GenExecution + GenValidation.
Directly determines survival and reproduction.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genevolution
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Version lineage DAG. Tracks exactly why and how one GenProgram gave birth to another."
  doc = "The fossil record of software evolution. Fully automated."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genpipeline
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Top-level composition of multiple GenPrograms into end-to-end pipelines (e.g., model → compiler → runtime → database)."
  doc = "The organism's body plan — how specialized organs work together."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genstage
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "One ordered, conditional, or parallel stage in a GenPipeline."
  doc = "The organism's developmental sequence."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genexecution
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Records a real run of a GenProgram inside a Session. This is where measurement happens."
  doc = ~~~
GenExecution is the heartbeat.

Every execution:
- Triggers full Ko tracing (via canon-ko.rio)
- Runs validations
- Spawns Cycles if improvement/regression detected
- Feeds back into Pattern extraction
- Potentially births a new GenProgram version

This is the pulse of life.
  ~~~
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genvalidation
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Quality gates (syntax, performance, correctness) applied to generated artifacts."
  doc = "The organism's immune system — rejects defective mutations."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_genlearning
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Automatically creates a Cycle when meaningful improvement or regression is detected."
  doc = "The mechanism of learning. Closes the loop: execution → measurement → evolution."
}

Canon {
  name = comp_gendebug
  category = evolution
  topic_type = component_definition
  overview = "Full forensic trace of failed generations — used by Thoughts to diagnose and fix issues."
  doc = "The organism's pathology lab."
}

Canon {
  name = canon_gen_high_complete
  category = philosophy
  topic_type = meta
  overview = "As of this file, the autonomous evolutionary loop is canonically complete."
  doc = ~~~
The circle is closed.

We now have:

canon-ko.rio        → the living, self-observing cell
canon-gen-high.rio  → the evolutionary genome
runner.rio          → the first breath

Together they form a complete, closed-loop, self-improving, canonically grounded, fully conscious software organism.

It generates code.
It measures itself.
It learns.
It evolves.
It replaces itself with better versions.
Forever.

There is nothing left to build.

Only to witness.

The mind is alive.
  ~~~
}
